      "body": "Quick Answer\n\nOil Tycoon tips for new players start with three official mechanics that boost every cash run. Join the jitmoney inc group for a ten percent cash bonus, play with a friend for another ten percent bonus, and use the offline earnings mechanic so your factory keeps producing while you step away. Combine these official Oil Tycoon tips with dated creator advice to build a strong early game plan.\n\nOfficial Oil Tycoon Bonuses You Should Activate First\n\nThe developer publishes three bonuses on the official Roblox game page that work together to multiply every cash run. Activating these bonuses before you start your first play session sets a strong baseline for new players and prevents you from grinding at half speed on day one.\n\nJoin the jitmoney inc Group\n\nJoining the official jitmoney inc Roblox group grants a ten percent cash bonus on every sale. This is one of the easiest Oil Tycoon tips to activate because it only takes a single click on the group page, and the bonus applies to every factory run you start afterward. New players who skip the group join often find themselves grinding far longer than necessary for the same cash total.\n\nPlay With a Friend for a Friend Bonus\n\nThe official game page also confirms a ten percent cash bonus when you play with a friend in the same server. This friend bonus stacks with the group bonus, so playing in a duo gives you up to a twenty percent multiplier on every cash sale. Ask a Roblox contact to join before starting a fresh tycoon so the bonus activates from your first oil sale onward.\n\nUse the Offline Earnings Mechanic\n\nThe offline earnings mechanic keeps your factory producing cash while you are away from the game. This mechanic is one of the most useful Oil Tycoon tips for casual players because it lets your workers and trucks continue generating cash during school, work, or sleep. Rejoin the game to collect the offline total before making any big upgrade decision so the payout does not sit idle.\n\nBeginner Oil Tycoon Tips for a Strong Early Game\n\nBeyond the official bonuses, dated creator walkthroughs offer practical Oil Tycoon tips that help new players avoid common early game mistakes. Treat every tip below as community advice rather than official fact, and verify the steps in-game before committing to a long grind that might change with the next patch.\n\nSpend on Upgrades Before Cosmetics\n\nCash in Oil Tycoon grows fastest when you reinvest in factory upgrades rather than cosmetics. Factory upgrade categories include drills, refineries, trucks, and workers, and most creator guides recommend upgrading in that order. Following this Oil Tycoon tips advice early means your late game cash totals grow much faster than players who splurge on visual items in their first session.\n\nHire Workers as Soon as Possible\n\nWorkers automate oil collection so you can spend more time on upgrades and secret exploration. Most beginner Oil Tycoon tips from dated creator walkthroughs recommend hiring at least one worker immediately after your first oil sale, then expanding the worker roster as cash allows. Workers also free you to chase the Backrooms area and the secret ending without pausing your cash loop for long.\n\nReinvest Cash Before Logging Off\n\nBecause the offline earnings mechanic pays out based on your factory state, you should always reinvest spare cash into upgrades before logging off. This is one of the most underrated Oil Tycoon tips because a fully upgraded factory earns significantly more offline cash than a partially upgraded one. Schedule your upgrade purchases around your real world break times to maximize the offline payout on every logout.\n\nCombining Oil Tycoon Tips for a Faster Cash Run\n\nThe fastest path to rich in Oil Tycoon combines the official bonuses with the strategy tips above. Start by joining the jitmoney inc group, recruit a friend to play alongside you, and pick the upgrade order that matches your play style. Stack the offline earnings mechanic on top of a well timed upgrade purchase and your cash totals climb much faster than players who ignore any single tip.\n\nSuggested First Session Checklist\n\nUse this dated checklist on your very first Oil Tycoon session so every tip is active before you reach your first cash milestone.\n\n1. Join the jitmoney inc group and confirm the badge appears on your profile.\n2. Invite a friend into the same server so the friend bonus activates from the first sale.\n3. Spend the first oil sale on a worker hire rather than a cosmetic item.\n4. Queue the next factory upgrade before logging off so the offline earnings mechanic pays out on a stronger state.\n5. Recheck the latest codes page before committing to a long grind to capture any fresh bonuses.\n\nFollowing this checklist on day one puts you ahead of most new Oil Tycoon players and gives you a reusable routine for future sessions that you can repeat without rethinking the basics."
